      "contentSections": [
        {
          "type": "tier-comparison",
          "title": "QMB vs SLMB vs QI: Which Program Fits Your Parent?",
          "content": "**QMB (Qualified Medicare Beneficiary)**, Income up to $1,330/month (single): Covers Part B premium ($202.90/month), all deductibles, copays, and coinsurance. Providers cannot bill your loved one for covered services.\n\n**SLMB (Specified Low-Income Medicare Beneficiary)**, Income $1,330-$1,596/month (single): Covers Part B premium only ($202.90/month, $2,435/year savings).\n\n**QI (Qualifying Individual)**, Income $1,596-$1,796/month (single): Covers Part B premium only ($202.90/month, $2,435/year savings). Limited funding, first-come first-served."
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "title": "Asset Counting: What's Included and Exempt",
          "content": "**Counted toward $9,950 limit**: Bank accounts, certificates of deposit, stocks, bonds, mutual funds, second vehicles, cash value of life insurance over certain amounts.\n\n**Exempt (not counted)**: Your loved one's primary home regardless of value, one vehicle, burial plots, burial funds up to $1,500 per person, personal belongings, irrevocable burial trusts."
        }
      ],
      "faqs": [
        {
          "question": "Can my loved one keep their house if it's worth more than the asset limit?",
          "answer": "Yes. The primary residence is completely exempt from the $9,950 asset limit regardless of value. Only countable assets like bank accounts, investments, and second vehicles count toward the limit."
        },
        {
          "question": "What if my loved one's income is just over the limit by a small amount?",
          "answer": "They may still qualify because North Carolina applies a $20 general income disregard. So if your loved one's income is $1,350/month, only $1,330 counts, which is within the QMB limit. Always apply if income is close to the limits."
        },
        {
          "question": "Can I apply for my loved one if they have dementia or can't handle paperwork?",
          "answer": "Yes. Family members can apply on behalf of elderly loved ones, especially those with cognitive impairment. You may need to provide power of attorney documentation or become an authorized representative through the county DSS office."
        },
        {
          "question": "How is the QI waitlist handled if funding runs out?",
          "answer": "QI operates first-come, first-served with limited federal funding that may exhaust before year-end. If funding runs out, new applications go on a waiting list for the next calendar year. Apply in January or February for the best chance."
        },
        {
          "question": "What happens if my loved one gets approved for QMB but providers still send bills?",
          "answer": "Providers are legally prohibited from billing QMB beneficiaries for covered Medicare services. Keep the MSP identification card handy, contact the provider's billing department to show QMB status, and report persistent billing issues to your county DSS office."
        },
        {
          "question": "Can my loved one apply for Medicare Savings Programs and regular Medicaid at the same time?",
          "answer": "No. Medicare Savings Programs are specifically for Medicare beneficiaries who don't qualify for full Medicaid due to income or assets being slightly too high. If your loved one qualifies for full Medicaid, they would get that instead."
        },
        {
          "question": "How often does my loved one need to renew their Medicare Savings Program benefits?",
          "answer": "Renewals are typically required annually, similar to other Medicaid programs. Your county DSS office will send renewal paperwork before benefits expire. QI beneficiaries must reapply each year regardless due to the program's annual funding structure."
        },
        {
          "question": "Will Medicare Savings Programs automatically sign my loved one up for Extra Help with prescriptions?",
          "answer": "Yes. All three programs (QMB, SLMB, QI) automatically qualify your loved one for the full Extra Help benefit for Medicare Part D prescription costs. However, verify this enrollment is active by checking with Medicare at (800) 633-4227."
        }
      ],
