      "intro": "If your loved one is 60+ and homebound due to illness or disability, county meal delivery programs can bring nutritious meals directly to their door. Because your loved one can't shop or prepare food safely, these programs provide regular home-delivered meals at no cost to help them stay nourished and independent.\n\nEach county in North Carolina runs its own program independently, Pender, Haywood, Mecklenburg, Brunswick, Onslow, and Caldwell counties have documented programs. Because there's no statewide system, eligibility requirements and application processes vary by county, though all require your loved one to be homebound and unable to obtain or prepare food.\n\nAll programs maintain waiting lists, so expect delays between application and meal delivery. Contact your county's Area Agency on Aging or Department of Social Services to find your local program and verify current availability.",
