      "intro": "If your loved one is 55+ and unemployed with limited income, SCSEP provides part-time paid job training (about 20 hours/week) at minimum wage while building skills for permanent employment. Your loved one works at community host sites like schools, hospitals, or senior centers in roles such as teacher's aide, customer service, or maintenance worker while receiving training and job placement assistance.\n\nThis is a bridge program, typically lasting 6 months, designed to help participants transition to unsubsidized employment. Your loved one earns a paycheck during training while developing marketable skills like computer literacy, customer service, or specialized job training. Veterans and their spouses get priority placement, followed by those over 65, with disabilities, or facing barriers to employment.",
