      "intro": "If your loved one is 60 or older in North Carolina, they can get free civil legal help with essential issues like writing wills, obtaining benefits, preventing eviction, and stopping financial abuse. Legal Aid of North Carolina's Senior Law Project provides legal advice, document review, advocacy letters, and referrals to local attorneys at no cost, regardless of your loved one's income or assets.\n\nThe program handles the legal issues that most threaten seniors' safety and independence: Medicaid and SNAP applications, wrongful evictions, consumer scams, unemployment compensation, and powers of attorney. Because seniors 60+ are exempt from all income limits, your loved one qualifies for help based on age alone, though priority goes to those with the greatest economic or social need.",
