      "intro": "If your loved one needs daily help with bathing, dressing, or medication management, North Carolina Long-Term Care Medicaid can cover the full cost of nursing home care, assisted living, or home-based services. Your loved one pays most of their income toward care costs (keeping only $70/month for personal needs), and Medicaid covers the remainder, which can be $8,000–$11,000/month for nursing home care depending on the facility.\n\nTo qualify, your loved one must have less than $2,000 in countable assets (singles) or $3,000 (married couples both needing care), plus income below the regional nursing home pay rate (estimated $7,898–$11,218/month in 2026). They can keep their home if equity is under $752,000 and they intend to return, or if a spouse or disabled child lives there. Because this program requires a clinical assessment proving need for daily care, the application takes 45–90 days including the functional evaluation.",
